WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.106
Hi! Yesterday I went to the park. When something has already happened, the verb changes. Today we'll learn the simple past tense.

2
00:00:11.256 --> 00:00:16.602
Words like yesterday, last week and two days ago tell us to use the past tense.

3
00:00:16.752 --> 00:00:19.962
Most verbs add ed: walked, played.

4
00:00:20.112 --> 00:00:23.802
Verbs ending in e just add d: baked, liked.

5
00:00:23.952 --> 00:00:30.546
Consonant plus y: change y to i and add ed: cried, carried.

6
00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:34.626
Some verbs change in special ways: went, saw.

7
00:00:34.776 --> 00:00:38.226
Eat becomes ate, and run becomes ran.

8
00:00:38.376 --> 00:00:41.634
Is becomes was, and are becomes were.

9
00:00:41.784 --> 00:00:48.090
In the negative, I did not go: after did not, use the base verb.

10
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.026
Watch out! The past of go is not goed!

11
00:00:52.176 --> 00:00:56.226
Go is irregular. Its past tense is went.

12
00:00:56.376 --> 00:01:00.498
So it's Yesterday we went to the zoo.

13
00:01:00.648 --> 00:01:10.386
Your turn! Yesterday I, ___, football. Which one? Pause and think.

14
00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:16.290
Yesterday means the past: played. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:26.274
Another one! Mum, ___, a cake last Sunday. Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:26.424 --> 00:01:32.298
Bake ends in e, so add d: baked. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:32.448 --> 00:01:42.210
Here's another! We, ___, a rainbow this morning. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:47.346
The past of see is saw. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:47.496 --> 00:01:57.090
Try one more! The baby, ___, last night. Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:03.114
Change y to i and add ed: cried. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:03.264 --> 00:02:14.298
Try one more! I, ___, noodles for lunch. Lunch is over. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:14.448 --> 00:02:19.818
It already happened, so ate. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:31.170
Try one more! They, ___, happy at the party. The party is over. Which one? Pause and think.

24
00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:36.354
The past of are is were. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:36.504 --> 00:02:45.810
Last one! He did not, ___, the bus. Which one? Pause and think.

26
00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:52.458
After did not, use the base verb: miss. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:52.608 --> 00:03:02.298
Remember: use the past tense for things that already happened. Most verbs add ed; learn the irregular ones: went, saw, ate.

28
00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:06.089
Say what you did yesterday!

